421
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:00,640
All right, so moving on.

422
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:03,720
Present discounted value diversification and risk premium.

423
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,680
So in a world of total certainty,

424
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:09,120
every asset has to sell for its present discounted value.

425
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:11,920
So remember present discounted values.

426
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:15,280
So remember those?

427
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:17,680
In a world of certainty, every asset will sell for that.

428
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:20,960
Because any asset that is selling for below its present

429
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:24,640
discounted value is an arbitrage opportunity to go and buy it.

430
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:27,200
Anything selling for more than its present discounted value

431
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,560
is an arbitrage opportunity to sell it short.

432
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:32,640
And so the only stable result is the equal

433
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:34,960
of present discounted value.

434
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:37,920
And if we've got risk-neutral agents,

435
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,800
so either everyone's risk-averse or the marginal person

436
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:43,080
is risk-averse, then actually this

437
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:45,480
holds under uncertainty.

438
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:50,160
Then everything sells for its expected present discounted

439
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:51,240
value.

440
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:53,680
If we've got either everyone risk-averse

441
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:57,160
or we've got at least the marginal agent risk-averse,

442
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:59,600
because again, if the marginal agent is risk-averse,

443
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,960
then any time something is selling above or below

444
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:04,160
the expected present discounted value,

445
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:06,960
they will either just buy it or sell it short.

446
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,160
And you say, oh, it's risky.

447
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:10,120
He's like, yeah, but I don't worry about risk.

448
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:10,920
I'm just neutral.

449
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:13,720
So no problem.

450
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:16,800
But once we've got enough risk-averse agents

451
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:18,640
that the marginal person isn't risk-averse,

452
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,120
the world is risk-averse.

453
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:23,040
So once we get to that world, which almost everyone thinks

454
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:25,520
is the actual world, so the marginal person

455
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:28,840
is actually risk-averse, then the present discounted value

456
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:32,600
is no longer the sole determinant of an asset's price.

457
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:34,680
It's always important, but it's no longer

458
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,560
the sole determinant.

459
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:38,440
Instead, what we expect is that things

460
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:40,960
are going to sell for their expected present discounted

461
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:45,920
value minus some risk discount.

462
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:52,720
Or we can also say that everything

463
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:58,160
earns the normal return plus a risk premium.

464
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:03,680
How can one asset sell for risk discount

465
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:06,240
but earn a risk premium?

466
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:08,320
Was that possible?

467
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:10,320
Well, this is exactly the same thing as, look,

